  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final v35 keeps numerical per-model test results confidential to regulators and to purchasers, with no public posting, which satisfies both companies' stated red lines. The S2 sales-stop is removed: a 5% exceedance triggers corrective action and retesting but never mandates market exclusion, which favours Northwind's flagship Hearth 10 (6.2%). The 8-per-100k mandatory recall trigger applies immediately with no transition, which directly exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k)."
